Correctness and API safety:
- matrix2/3/4_invert silently leave the matrix unchanged when it is singular (see matrix4_invert);
  return a status the caller can check, or document the behavior clearly
- Answer the SLERP shortest-arc question above with a test, then fix if needed
- Test quaternion inverse with non-unit quaternions (see above) and fix if needed
- HYP_EPSILON is a fixed absolute 1E-5 for both float and double builds; consider a
  precision-specific value and/or relative / ULP-based comparisons for large magnitudes

C89 compliance:
- `gcc -std=c89 -pedantic` reports 34 warnings: 25 unnamed structs/unions, 7 structs with
  no named members, 2 anonymous variadic macros
- <stdint.h> / uint8_t are C99
- Either provide a strict-C89 path (feature macro for the anonymous unions, replace uint8_t)
  or change the README to say "C99, C89-friendly style"

Experimental (_EXP) functions:
- Add reference-value tests (e.g. against GLM output) for projection_perspective_fovy_rh,
  projection_ortho3d_rh, view_lookat_rh, rotate_by_euler_angles, transformation_decompose,
  quaternion_angle_between
- Add left-handed variants of the projection / view functions
- Add a depth-range option: 0..1 (Vulkan/D3D) vs -1..1 (OpenGL)
- Once tested, promote them and drop the _EXP suffix

